<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Espiritu Santo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Espiritu Santo is the largest island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vanuatu">Vanuatu</a>, in the south-west Pacific; its main town is Luganville. It was named by the navigator Pedro Fernandes de Queirós, who landed there in 1606 believing he had found the great southern continent. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> it became a major American naval and air base, and in 1980 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagriamel">Nagriamel</a> movement of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jimmy-stevens">Jimmy Stevens</a> tried to make it secede on the eve of Vanuatu's independence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/espiritu-santo.jpg" alt="Espiritu Santo" width="320" height="350" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: United States Bureau of Yards and Docks · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Espiritu_Santo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
